  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Saraj @ Seraj Ansari vs The State Of Jharkhand .... Opposite ... on 7 June, 2018 Author: Rajesh Kumar Bench: Rajesh Kumar In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi B. A. No. 4538 of 2018 .... 1. Saraj @ Seraj Ansari 2. Najrul Ansari .... Petitioners Versus The State of Jharkhand .... Opposite Party .... Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Rajesh Kumar For the Petitioners : Mr. Sidhartha Roy, Adv.",
    "facts": "The applicants have prayed for regular bail in connection with Penk Narayanpur P.S. Case No. 41 of 2017 corresponding to G.R. No. 798 of 2017 registered under Section 429/406/188/120-B IPC, Sections 11(a), (d), (e), (i), (k) of Animal Cruelty Prohibition Act, 1960, Section 3 of Animal Slaughter Act, 2001 and Section 55 of Food and Safety Standard Act. It is alleged that 10 unclaimed camels were seized and was entrusted to different persons. Later on, after Bakrid the camels were not produced and also those persons did not appear before the authority. It is alleged that those persons may have sacrificed the camels during Bakrid. It is submitted by the learned counsel for the applicant that co-accused namely Shahid Ansari @ Md. Shahid Ansari has been granted bail vide B.A. No. 8517 of 2017 by the Hon'ble coordinate Bench of this Court. Learned APP has opposed the prayer for bail.",
